  "headword": "{完治|かんち}",
  "reading": "かんち",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "complete recovery, full cure",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "complete recovery, full cure, complete healing",
      "explanation": "A disease or injury being fully cured with no remaining symptoms. Used in medical contexts to indicate that treatment has been completely successful."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "12268_kanchi_ex1",
      "japanese": "{病気|びょうき}が{完治|かんち}した。",
      "english": "The illness was completely cured.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "12268_kanchi_ex2",
      "japanese": "{完治|かんち}するまでに{半年|はんとし}かかった。",
      "english": "It took half a year to fully recover.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "12268_kanchi_ex3",
      "japanese": "この{病気|びょうき}は{早期|そうき}{発見|はっけん}すれば{完治|かんち}できる{可能性|かのうせい}が{高|たか}い。",
      "english": "If this disease is detected early, there is a high possibility of a complete cure.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "USAGE:\nA medical term indicating that a condition has been fully resolved. Used as a suru verb: {完治|かんち}する (to be completely cured). Often contrasted with situations where symptoms are managed but not eliminated.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{全快|ぜんかい} also means complete recovery but tends to emphasize the patient's return to full health, while {完治|かんち} emphasizes the disease or injury itself being fully cured.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {完治|かんち}する: to be completely cured\n- {完治|かんち}が{難|むずか}しい: difficult to cure completely\n- {完治|かんち}を{目指|めざ}す: to aim for a complete cure\n- {完治|かんち}までの{期間|きかん}: period until full recovery",
